[5.1375, "o", "                   \u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m Requests allows you to send HTTP/1.1 requests  \u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;136mMaintainer Email\u001b[0m: Ian Stapleton Cordasco       \u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m extremely easily. There\u2019s no need to manually  \u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m <graffatcolmingov@gmail.com>, Nate Prewitt     \u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m add query strings to your URLs, or to          \u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m <nate.prewitt@gmail.com>                       \u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m form-encode your \u001b[97;40mPUT\u001b[0m & \u001b[97;40mPOST\u001b[0m data \u2014 but         \u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;136mRequires Python\u001b[0m: >=3.10                        \u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m nowadays, just use the \u001b[97;40mjson\u001b[0m method!            \u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;136mOwner #1:\u001b[0m Lukasa                               \u001b[38;5;226m\u2502\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m                                                \u001b[1;35m\u2502\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;226m\u2502"]
